DL4 is fairly deep for a lvl5 char, especially if you're not a big
fighting type.  If you do have to take them on, it's important to
position yourself so only one can be fighting you at a time; standing
behind a doorway is good, and if you have a wand and can line them up
in a corridor, even better.

Unless you've picked up some better equipment, I'd recommend descending
a DL for every 2 char levels.  The RNG "helpfully" provides additional
monsters for you to fight in the interim, you may just have to get used
to the taste of jackal or be prepared to call on your god when nearly
dead of starvation :)  Patience is the key.



